    "q-67871": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67871",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "In a quadrilateral $ABCD,$ the measures of the sides are $AB=17\\,mm,$ $BC=14\\,mm,$ $CD=2\\,cm,$ and $DA=9\\,mm.$\nWhat is the perimeter of the quadrilateral?",
      "worked_solution": "Most of the measures are given in $mm$ (millimeters), so we will start by converting all the measures to $mm$ and adding them up:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =17\\,mm+14\\,mm+\\overset{2\\,cm}{\\overset{⏞}{20\\,mm}}+9\\,mm \\\\  & =60\\,mm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is a large quantity of $\\text{mm},$ we will convert to $\\text{cm}:$\n\n$$\np=60\\,mm=6\\,cm.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
